q: "Q13. Which mountain vegetation belt features coniferous trees like pine, deodar, and fir at elevations between 1,500m and 3,000m in the Himalayas?\nहिमालयी क्षेत्रों में 1500 से 3000 मीटर की ऊंचाई पर पाए जाने वाले शंकुधारी वनों (चीड़, देवदार, फर) को क्या कहा जाता है?",
options: ["A) Montane Forests / Alpine and Coniferous Forests (पर्वतीय / शंकुधारी वन)", "B) Tropical Deciduous forests", "C) Thorn scrublands", "D) Mangroves"],
answer: 0,
exp: "Explanation / स्पष्टीकरण:\n• **Montane forests** change with altitude in the Himalayas, transitioning from deciduous to temperate broadleaf, and coniferous (*pine, deodar, fir*) at higher elevations."
