q: "Q18. What is the difference between an 'Ascribed Status' and an 'Achieved Status'?\n'प्रदत्त स्थिति' (Ascribed Status) और 'अर्जित स्थिति' (Achieved Status) में क्या अंतर है?",
options: ["A) Ascribed status is assigned at birth (like caste or sex), whereas achieved status is earned through personal effort and skills (like doctor or engineer)\n(प्रदत्त स्थिति जन्म से मिलती है जैसे जाति या लिंग, जबकि अर्जित स्थिति व्यक्ति अपनी योग्यता से प्राप्त करता है)", "B) Both statuses are assigned purely by random government lottery", "C) Achieved status is inherited from grandparents automatically", "D) Ascribed status requires passing university examinations"],
answer: 0,
exp: "Explanation / स्पष्टीकरण:\n• An **ascribed status** is social position received involuntarily at birth (race, caste, gender), while an **achieved status** is earned through individual effort, merit, and skill (profession, education)."
