q: "Q24. What is the difference between 'Material Culture' and 'Non-Material Culture'?\n'भौतिक संस्कृति' (Material Culture) और 'अभौतिक संस्कृति' (Non-Material Culture) में क्या अंतर है?",
options: ["A) Material culture consists of physical objects created by humans (buildings, tools), while non-material consists of intangible creations (beliefs, values, norms)\n(भौतिक संस्कृति दृश्य और निर्मित वस्तुएं हैं, जबकि अभौतिक संस्कृति में विचार, मूल्य और विश्वास आते हैं)", "B) Material culture is ancient, non-material culture is modern", "C) Material culture belongs to villages, non-material to cities", "D) There is no distinction"],
answer: 0,
exp: "Explanation / स्पष्टीकरण:\n• **Material culture** includes physical, tangible human-made objects (tools, clothing, architecture), whereas **non-material culture** consists of abstract intangible creations (values, beliefs, language, social rules)."
