q: "Q28. What is the significance of the Von Neumann architecture in modern computer design?\nआधुनिक कंप्यूटर डिज़ाइन में 'वॉन न्यूमैन आर्किटेक्चर' (Von Neumann Architecture) का क्या ऐतिहासिक महत्व है?\n",
options: ["A) Introduced the stored-program concept where data and instruction programs are stored in the same electronic memory\n(संग्रहित-प्रोग्राम अवधारणा, जिसमें डेटा और निर्देश एक ही मेमोरी में स्टोर होते हैं)", "B) Banned all RAM memory chips from computers", "C) Replaced CPU arithmetic with mechanical gears", "D) Eliminated operating systems entirely"],
answer: 0,
exp: "Explanation / स्पष्टीकरण:\n• John von Neumann proposed the **stored-program computer** architecture, where data and program instructions are stored together in read-write memory, forming the blueprint of modern computers."
